  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOR participation International workshop on Salinity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Across the world freshwater scarcity and soil salinisation are putting increasing pressure on agriculture, food security and water management. These challenges demand more than theory, they call for practical, field-tested solutions and strong international collaboration. The purpose of this project is to facilitate the participation of three experts from the Moroccan Institut National de la Recherche Agronomique (INRA) in the Institute for Agriculture in Salinizing Deltas (SALTA) International Workshop. During the workshop experts, farmers, researchers, policymakers and innovators from around the globe will come together in Leeuwarden, the Netherlands, to exchange knowledge and accelerate real-world action. This project fits well within the objectives of the combi-track to make Moroccan agriculture more efficient and resilient against climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
